  "note": "Annual election of one third (five seats), Friday 15 January 1915, for the places of H. G. MacGeagh, D.L., John Mahaffy, J.P., Thomas L. Cole, George McGhee and Maxwell Thompson (who did not seek re-election); six candidates, one more than the seats, so that (as the Lurgan Mail of 9 January 1915 put it) a walk-over was averted by one candidate. \"Out of an electorate of 2,435 some 1,313 had exercised\" the franchise, more than 800 in the last three hours, many of them soldiers of the Ulster Division given leave to vote; \"There were only three spoiled votes.\" George McGhee (Nationalist in 1912) lost his seat. No party labels printed."
